  "goodToKnow": "Die Kolonie is a colony. Imperial Germany had colonies from 1884 until 1919, including today's Namibia, Tanzania, Cameroon and Togo; in Namibia, German troops committed genocide against the Herero and Nama (1904–1908), which Germany officially acknowledged in 2021. Today, die Kolonie also means a group of animals (eine Ameisenkolonie) and, in Berlin, a Kleingartenkolonie, a cluster of allotment gardens. Plural: die Kolonien."
